contract.content:
{
  "action": "execute",
  "archetype": "ai-tool",
  "message": "We'll build an internal policy Q&A assistant. Employees chat in plain English and get answers with citations linking back to the original SharePoint policy documents. Admins configure which SharePoint sites and libraries get indexed, and see a dashboard of top questions, usage trends, and content gaps. Documents are ingested and re-indexed on a schedule, chunked, embedded, and stored in pgvector for retrieval-augmented answers.",
  "flags": ["has-users", "has-admin", "ai-rag", "sharepoint"],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "scope": "database",
      "summary": "Stores users, configured SharePoint sources, ingested documents, and the Q&A history that powers the admin analytics.",
      "task": "Tables: users, sources, documents, questions, answers. Indexes: documents(source_id), questions(user_id, created_at DESC), answers(question_id). Column-level contract: data_model. FK ordering enforced. No extensions here (pgvector lives in vectordb scope).",
      "dockerfile": "Dockerfile.postgres",
      "rules": [],
      "snippets": [],
      "primarySnippet": ""
    },
    {
      "scope": "vectordb",
      "summary": "Holds embeddings of chunked SharePoint policy documents so the assistant can retrieve the most relevant passages for any question.",
      "task": "pgvector extension. Table: doc_chunks(id SERIAL PK, document_id INTEGER, source_id INTEGER, chunk_text TEXT, chunk_index INTEGER, sharepoint_url TEXT, embedding vector(3072), created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()). Index: HNSW on embedding (vector_cosine_ops). Embedding model: text-embedding-3-large via MGA.",
      "dockerfile": "Dockerfile.pgvector",
      "rules": [],
      "snippets": [],
      "primarySnippet": "vectordb/vectordb-connections.ts"
    },
    {
      "scope": "backend",
      "summary": "Express API that handles chat questions, runs retrieval-augmented answers via MGA with citations, manages SharePoint source config, and serves admin analytics.",
      "task": "Data: pg Pool from env; separate pgvector Pool on port 5433. Endpoints + bodies: api_contract. Behaviors + rules + side-effects: business_logic_contract. Auth: x-amzn-oidc-data JWT sub/email; auto-provision users row on first call; role='admin' gates /admin/*. Chat flow: embed question (text-embedding-3-large) → top-k cosine search on doc_chunks → call MGA assistant with retrieved chunks → return answer with citations[] (document title + sharepoint_url + chunk excerpt). Ingestion: scheduled job (node-cron) pulls SharePoint sources, chunks text, embeds, upserts. Validation on all POST/PUT bodies. Parameterised SQL. Uniform {error} responses with 400/403/404. List endpoints paginated (?limit=50&offset=0), newest-first.",
      "dockerfile": "Dockerfile.node",
      "rules": [],
      "snippets": [],
      "primarySnippet": "backend/express-server-template.ts"
    },
    {
      "scope": "frontend",
      "summary": "React chat interface for employees plus an admin console for managing SharePoint sources and viewing usage analytics.",
      "task": "Views + components: ui_contract. Endpoints + body shapes: api_contract (prepend /api/). Chat view is primary: message thread, input box, streamed/awaited assistant replies, inline citation chips that open the source SharePoint URL in a new tab. Admin route guarded by role from /whoami. States: spinner, empty CTA, toast on 4xx/5xx, 404 page, disabled submit during POST. Responsive.",
      "dockerfile": "Dockerfile.react",
      "rules": [],
      "snippets": [],
      "primarySnippet": "frontend/AppScaffold.tsx"
    },
    {
      "scope": "integration",
      "summary": "Wires the database, pgvector, backend, and frontend together for local dev and deploy.",
      "task": "Wire database, vectordb, backend, frontend. Backend env: DATABASE_HOST=database, DATABASE_PORT=5432, DATABASE_NAME=policyqa, DATABASE_USER=policyqa_user, DATABASE_PASSWORD=localdev123, VECTORDB_HOST=vectordb, VECTORDB_PORT=5433, VECTORDB_NAME=policyqa_vec, VECTORDB_USER=policyqa_user, VECTORDB_PASSWORD=localdev123. nginx.local.conf proxy /api→backend:3000. depends_on chain: frontend→backend→{database,vectordb}. Healthchecks on all services. Named volumes per db service.",
      "dockerfile": "",
      "rules": [],
      "snippets": [],
      "primarySnippet": "integration/docker-compose-fullstack.yml"
    }
  ],
  "data_model": {
    "tables": [
      {
        "name": "users",
        "columns": [
          {"name": "id", "type": "SERIAL PRIMARY KEY"},
          {"name": "oidc_sub", "type": "TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "email", "type": "VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "role", "type": "VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'employee'"},
          {"name": "created_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "sources",
        "columns": [
          {"name": "id", "type": "SERIAL PRIMARY KEY"},
          {"name": "name", "type": "VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "sharepoint_site_url", "type": "TEXT NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "library_name", "type": "VARCHAR(255)"},
          {"name": "enabled", "type": "BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE"},
          {"name": "last_indexed_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP"},
          {"name": "created_by", "type": "INTEGER REFERENCES users(id)"},
          {"name": "created_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "documents",
        "columns": [
          {"name": "id", "type": "SERIAL PRIMARY KEY"},
          {"name": "source_id", "type": "INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES sources(id) ON DELETE CASCADE"},
          {"name": "title", "type": "VARCHAR(512) NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "sharepoint_url", "type": "TEXT NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "content_hash", "type": "TEXT"},
          {"name": "indexed_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "questions",
        "columns": [
          {"name": "id", "type": "SERIAL PRIMARY KEY"},
          {"name": "user_id", "type": "INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id)"},
          {"name": "question_text", "type": "TEXT NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "created_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()"}
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "answers",
        "columns": [
          {"name": "id", "type": "SERIAL PRIMARY KEY"},
          {"name": "question_id", "type": "INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES questions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE"},
          {"name": "answer_text", "type": "TEXT NOT NULL"},
          {"name": "citations", "type": "JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'"},
          {"name": "had_results", "type": "BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE"},
          {"name": "created_at", "type": "TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()"}
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "api_contract": {
    "version": 1,
    "endpoints": [
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/whoami",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ id, email, role }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/chat/ask",
        "request": {"question_text": "string required"},
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ question_id, answer_text, citations: [{ document_id, title, sharepoint_url, excerpt }] }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/chat/history",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ items: [{ question_id, question_text, answer_text, citations, created_at }], limit, offset }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/documents/:id",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ id, title, sharepoint_url, source_id }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/admin/sources",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ items: [{ id, name, sharepoint_site_url, library_name, enabled, last_indexed_at }] }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/sources",
        "request": {"name": "string required", "sharepoint_site_url": "string required", "library_name": "string optional", "enabled": "boolean optional"},
        "response": {"status": 201, "body": "{ id, name, sharepoint_site_url, library_name, enabled }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/admin/sources/:id",
        "request": {"name": "string optional", "sharepoint_site_url": "string optional", "library_name": "string optional", "enabled": "boolean optional"},
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ id, name, sharepoint_site_url, library_name, enabled }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/admin/sources/:id",
        "response": {"status": 204, "body": ""}
      },
      {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/admin/sources/:id/reindex",
        "response": {"status": 202, "body": "{ source_id, status }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/admin/analytics/top-questions",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ items: [{ question_text, count }] }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/admin/analytics/content-gaps",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ items: [{ question_text, count, last_asked_at }] }"}
      },
      {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/admin/analytics/usage",
        "response": {"status": 200, "body": "{ total_questions, unique_users, questions_per_day: [{ date, count }] }"}
      }
    ]
  },
  "ui_contract": {
    "primary_view": "chat conversation with the policy assistant",
    "primary_action": "ask a policy question in plain English",
    "secondary_views": [
      "chat history",
      "admin source configuration",
      "admin analytics dashboard"
    ],
    "components": [
      {"name": "ChatThread", "role": "scrolling list of user questions and assistant answers"},
      {"name": "ChatComposer", "role": "input box where the employee types a question and submits"},
      {"name": "AnswerBubble", "role": "renders an assistant answer with inline citation chips"},
      {"name": "CitationChip", "role": "clickable chip linking to the underlying SharePoint document"},
      {"name": "HistoryDrawer", "role": "previous questions the user has asked"},
      {"name": "AdminSourcesTable", "role": "list, add, edit, disable, and reindex SharePoint sources"},
      {"name": "SourceForm", "role": "form to add or edit a SharePoint site/library source"},
      {"name": "AnalyticsDashboard", "role": "top questions, usage trends, and content-gap panels"},
      {"name": "TopQuestionsPanel", "role": "ranked list of most-asked questions"},
      {"name": "ContentGapsPanel", "role": "questions where the assistant had no good source match"}
    ]
  },
  "business_logic_contract": {
    "triggers": [
      {"event": "user_first_login", "action": "create users row from OIDC claims (sub, email); default role='employee'"},
      {"event": "question_asked", "action": "persist question, embed question text via MGA text-embedding-3-large, top-k cosine search on doc_chunks, call MGA chat assistant with retrieved chunks, persist answer with citations referencing document_id + sharepoint_url"},
      {"event": "source_created_or_reindex_requested", "action": "enqueue ingestion job: pull docs from SharePoint site/library, chunk text, embed chunks, upsert documents + doc_chunks, set sources.last_indexed_at"},
      {"event": "scheduled_reindex_tick", "action": "for each enabled source, re-run ingestion job on a daily cron"}
    ],
    "rules": [
      "all authenticated employees may use /chat/* and read their own /chat/history",
      "users can only see their own chat history",
      "/admin/* endpoints require role='admin' — return 403 otherwise",
      "answers must always include citations[]; if no relevant chunks are retrieved, return an explicit 'no authoritative source found' answer and flag had_results=false so it surfaces in content-gap analytics",
      "citations must reference a real documents row with a valid sharepoint_url"
    ],
    "side_effects": [
      "every question/answer pair is persisted to power top-questions and content-gap analytics",
      "ingestion job updates sources.last_indexed_at on completion"
    ]
  },
  "mga_assistants": [
    {
      "key": "default",
      "name": "Policy Q&A Assistant",
      "description": "Answers employee questions about internal policies, procedures, and compliance using indexed SharePoint documents. Always cites authoritative sources; refuses to answer when no relevant source is found.",
      "model": "claude-opus-4.7",
      "tool_keys": [],
      "starter_messages": [
        "What is our policy on remote work?",
        "How do I submit an expense reimbursement?",
        "What are the data retention requirements for customer records?"
      ],
      "instructions": "Answer only from the provided retrieved policy chunks. Always include citations to the source documents. If retrieved context does not contain the answer, say so explicitly rather than guessing."
    }
  ]
}
